/* book exam traps: Counter-current does not give every stage a larger driving force: stage 1 meets solvent already at Y2. Its gain is that the extract leaves near equilibrium with the richest liquid, so each kilogram of solvent carries more solute. | The Kremser form with (ε − 1)/(εN+1 − 1) assumes pure entering solvent; for recycled solvent shift X by YN+1/K′. | Δ is not a real stream and often lies outside the triangle; lines RnEn+1 pass through it, tie lines do not. | Minimum solvent gives infinite stages, not zero stages. */
