/* book exam traps: The settler area depends on the flow of the continuous liquid through which the drops settle, and on the drop settling velocity; the mixer volume sets only the contact time. | Stokes' law needs Re below about 1; check it, and use the continuous-phase viscosity. | The packing must be wetted by the continuous phase; if the dispersed phase wets it, the drops spread into films and the area falls. | A spray column is not many stages: back-mixing of the continuous phase limits it to one or two. | Transfer units (NOR = 4.16) are not ideal stages; they become equal only when ε = 1. */
