/* book Worked example: Q: 1000 kg of seeds holding 20 mass% oil and 80 mass% inert meal is leached in one ideal stage with 500 kg of pure solvent. The underflow retains 0.5 kg of solution per kg of inert. Find the oil in the overflow and the recovery.
   1. Inert I = 0.80 × 1000 = 800 kg; oil AF = 200 kg; no liquid in the feed.
   2. Retained solution L = rI = 0.5 × 800 = 400 kg.
   3. All the oil dissolves: total solution M = 200 + 500 = 700 kg, y = 200/700 = 0.2857 kg oil per kg solution.
   4. Overflow V = M − L = 700 − 400 = 300 kg, carrying 300 × 0.2857 = 85.7 kg oil.
   5. Underflow: 800 kg inert + 400 kg solution with 400 × 0.2857 = 114.3 kg oil. Check: 85.7 + 114.3 = 200 kg.
   6. Recovery = 85.7/200 = 42.9 %.
   Answer: The overflow carries 85.7 kg of oil (42.9 % recovery); 114.3 kg stays in the wet meal. */
