/* book Worked example 2: Q: The underflow of the first example is leached again in a second ideal cross-current stage with another 500 kg of pure solvent. Find the total recovery. What would the same 500 kg have given if split into two portions of 250 kg?
   1. Stage 2 input: 800 kg inert with 400 kg solution holding 114.3 kg oil, plus 500 kg solvent. M2 = 900 kg, y2 = 114.3/900 = 0.1270.
   2. V2 = 900 − 400 = 500 kg carrying 63.5 kg oil; underflow keeps 400 × 0.1270 = 50.8 kg.
   3. Total recovered = 85.7 + 63.5 = 149.2 kg, recovery 74.6 % for 1000 kg of solvent.
   4. Split 250 + 250: stage 1 M = 450 kg, y1 = 0.4444, V1 = 50 kg with 22.2 kg oil; stage 2 has 177.8 kg oil in 650 kg, y2 = 0.2735, V2 = 250 kg with 68.4 kg oil.
   5. Recovery with the split = (22.2 + 68.4)/200 = 45.3 %, only a little above 42.9 %: when the underflow holds 400 kg of the solution, small portions are mostly soaked up by it.
   Answer: Two stages of 500 kg recover 74.6 %; the same 500 kg split in two recovers 45.3 %. */
